# Unicode in cells: wide characters, combining marks, grapheme clusters (mode 2027) and invalid UTF-8.
#
# Widths follow UAX #11 (East Asian Width: Wide and Fullwidth take two cells, Ambiguous is narrow
# outside an East Asian context). Grapheme clusters follow the terminal-unicode-core specification
# (contour-terminal/terminal-unicode-core), which defines what mode 2027 does; without the mode
# the behaviour for clusters is undefined there. Wormhole has the mode on from the start (RIS and
# DECSTR set it again), so the cases that look at a single code point at a time turn it off first.
# The width of a cluster beyond the specification's (spacing marks, conjuncts, VS15) follows UTS #51
# for emoji presentation and the Unicode data files for the scripts: see the cases that say so.

test a CJK character takes two cells
spec UAX #11: CJK ideographs have East Asian Width W
size 10 3
feed 日本
cell 1,1 text=日 width=2
cell 1,2 text= width=0
cell 1,3 text=本 width=2
cell 1,4 width=0
cursor 1,5
screen
|日本|

test a fullwidth letter takes two cells
spec UAX #11: U+FF21 has East Asian Width F
size 10 3
feed Ａb
cell 1,1 text=Ａ width=2
cell 1,3 text=b width=1
cursor 1,4

test a halfwidth katakana takes one cell
spec UAX #11: U+FF71 has East Asian Width H
size 10 3
feed ｱb
cell 1,1 text=ｱ width=1
cell 1,2 text=b width=1

test a Hangul syllable takes two cells
spec UAX #11: Hangul syllables have East Asian Width W
size 10 3
feed 한
cell 1,1 text=한 width=2
cursor 1,3

test an emoji with emoji presentation takes two cells
spec UAX #11 and UTS #51: Emoji_Presentation characters are Wide
size 10 3
feed 😀x
cell 1,1 text=😀 width=2
cell 1,3 text=x
cursor 1,4

test an ambiguous width character takes one cell
spec UAX #11: Ambiguous characters are narrow outside an East Asian context
size 10 3
feed ¡αb
cell 1,1 text=¡ width=1
cell 1,2 text=α width=1
cursor 1,4

test a combining mark joins the cell before it
convention a non-spacing mark (Mn) takes no cell of its own and is stored with its base character
size 10 3
feed e\u{301}x
cell 1,1 text=e\u{301} width=1
cell 1,2 text=x
cursor 1,3
screen
|e\u{301}x|

test several combining marks join one cell
convention non-spacing marks take no cell
