feed a\u{300}\u{323}b
cell 1,1 text=a\u{300}\u{323} width=1
cell 1,2 text=b

test a combining mark joins a wide character
convention non-spacing marks take no cell, also after a wide base
size 10 3
feed 日\u{301}x
cell 1,1 text=日\u{301} width=2
cell 1,3 text=x
cursor 1,4

test a narrow character over the first half of a wide one clears the second half
convention a wide character is never left with half of its cells
size 10 3
feed 日\e[1;1Hx
screen
|x|
cell 1,2 text=\s width=1

test a narrow character over the second half of a wide one clears the first half
convention a wide character is never left with half of its cells
size 10 3
feed 日\e[1;2Hx
screen
| x|
cell 1,1 text=\s width=1

test a wide character over a wide one at an offset clears both
convention a wide character is never left with half of its cells
size 10 3
feed 日本\e[1;2H語
screen
| 語|
cell 1,1 text=\s width=1
cell 1,4 text=\s width=1

test a wide character over two narrow ones
convention a wide character replaces the two cells it covers
size 10 3
feed abcd\e[1;2H日
screen
|a日d|

test erasing to the left through the second half removes the whole character
spec ECMA-48 EL: positions up to and including the cursor are erased
size 10 3
feed 日本\e[1;2H\e[1K
screen
|  本|

test erasing to the right from the second half removes the whole character
convention erasing never leaves half of a wide character
known-fail: alacritty – erasing from or over the second half of a wide character leaves its first half on screen
size 10 3
feed 日本\e[1;2H\e[K
screen
||

test erasing characters over half of a wide character removes the whole character
convention erasing never leaves half of a wide character
known-fail: alacritty – erasing from or over the second half of a wide character leaves its first half on screen
size 10 3
feed 日本\e[1;2H\e[X
screen
|  本|

